From: Pyra kernel work <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: ti: aess: keep OPP100 when no widget reports a level

The speakers have never played through the AESS; only the headset did.
The codec and the speaker amplifiers are not the cause: the direct McPDM
link (legacy_link=1) plays through them on the same boot, and the whole
DAPM path down to "Ext Spk" is powered while the AESS path is silent.

The cause is the firmware's OPP task network. omap_aess_pcm_open() selects
OPP100, but every DAPM stream event -- about four a second during playback
-- calls aess_opp_recalc_level(), which derives the level from
aess->opp.widget[]. Nothing in this tree's DAPM graph (0019) fills that in,
so the OR is 0 and the level comes out as

    (1 << (fls(0) - 1)) * 25

a shift by -1, which evaluates to 0 here. aess_opp_set_level(0) takes its
"decrease" branch, falls to the default case and writes OPP50 into
MAXTASKBYTESINSLOT. Read back during playback: 0x0c, and debugfs opp_level
reads 0. At OPP50 the DL1 (headset) path runs and the DL2 (handsfree) path
does not.

Proved by ear with the stream held open: MAXTASKBYTESINSLOT = 0x0c, both
speakers silent; write 0x10 (OPP100), both speakers play; back to 0x0c,
silent again. The headphones play in both.

Treat "no widget reported a level" as unknown and keep OPP100, which is
what the open path asked for. A tree whose topology does populate
opp.widget[] is unaffected.

---
diff -ru a/sound/soc/ti/aess/aess_opp.c b/sound/soc/ti/aess/aess_opp.c
--- a/sound/soc/ti/aess/aess_opp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/ti/aess/aess_opp.c
@@ -250,7 +250,17 @@
 			opp |= aess->opp.widget[OMAP_AESS_WIDGET(i)];
 		}
 	}
-	opp = (1 << (fls(opp) - 1)) * 25;
+	/*
+	 * If no widget reported a level: the DAPM graph in this tree carries no
+	 * OPP information, so that means "unknown", not "idle". Keep the full
+	 * task network: below OPP100 the firmware does not run the DL2
+	 * (handsfree) path and the speakers are silent. Also avoids the
+	 * shift by fls(0) - 1 = -1.
+	 */
+	if (opp)
+		opp = (1 << (fls(opp) - 1)) * 25;
+	else
+		opp = 100;
 
 	/* OPP requested outside AESS driver (e.g. McPDM) */
 	requested_opp = aess_opp_get_requested(aess);
